  "body": "## Description\n\nAffects `IOExtensionsKt.md5Hash` in `app/src/main/java/com/philkes/notallyx/utils/IOExtensions.kt`.\n\nToday, export verification hashes the source ZIP and reopened URI before comparing their bytes. I found these helpers used MD5, while the MessageDigest analysis rule accepts SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512, SHA256, SHA384, and SHA512.\n\nI changed the Context, File, and InputStream helpers to `sha256Hash` using SHA-256 and updated the export verification references, names, and messages. The streaming, null handling, retry flow, and byte comparison remain unchanged. I added tests confirming identical content produces equal digests, modified content produces different digests, and the standard \"abc\" test vector produces the published SHA-256 digest.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nI also added a test for it (`IOExtensionsTest.kt`). The project builds with this change (`:app:testDebugUnitTest`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Bras\u00edlia (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNone.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Refactor / Code cleanup\n- [ ] Dependency update\n- [ ] Documentation update\n\n## AI-Assisted Disclosure\n\nPlease select the statement that best describes the role of AI (e.g., ChatGPT, Claude, GitHub Copilot) in this PR:\n\n- [ ] **No AI was used** (written and designed entirely by human author).\n- [x] **AI-Assisted** (AI acted as a tool for boilerplate, autocomplete, or debugging, but a human authored/reviewed the logic and architecture).\n- [ ] **AI-Generated with Human Verification** (substantial portions generated by AI prompts, manually verified, tested, and validated by the author).\n- [ ] **Fully AI-Generated** (authored entirely or near-entirely by an autonomous AI agent or prompt with minimal human code modification).\n\n*If AI was used, briefly mention which tools and where (optional):*\n>\n\n---\n\n## Testing & Quality Checklist\n\n- [x] Code builds cleanly locally (`./gradlew assembleDebug` or similar). Ran `assembleDebug` and `:app:testDebugUnitTest`.\n- [x] Added or updated unit/instrumented tests if applicable.\n- [ ] Tested on a device or emulator (Android API Level: ___).\n- [x] No hardcoded secrets, API keys, or unintended debugging logs.\n\n## Screenshots / Screen Recordings (if applicable)\n\nn/a",
